    "done_when": "tests/test_working_reads_working_at_once.py writes a live pointer whose stored phase is starting, starts a live process for it that the test records by pid, appends one assistant record to its stream.jsonl, runs one watcher snapshot, then asserts a transition into working. A second case puts the assistant record only in resume-1.jsonl, asserting the same. A third asserts the live MCP view's row for that pointer carries phase working, naming the key it reads. A fourth holds a pointer whose stream has only a system record, asserting it still reads dispatched. Every process the test starts is terminated in a finally block, with the test asserting none survives. The first case fails at the base revision with no transition emitted (logged) and passes at the head. The negative control, in a scratch copy, restores the stored-phase read in the reducer; the first case fails, with the mutation on the red log's first line and an EXIT= line after pytest's output. The gate is the new test plus the existing test files that exercise the row reducer or the live view; it exits 0, or shows no added failing ids against the base, with both arms recorded as log paths under baseline_suite and after_suite, each ending in an EXIT= line. The test neither reads nor writes the real ~/.config/reckon.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "Plan a-stalled-row-says-whether-the-worker-lives §7: a working worker reads working within one poll. Read §7 in docs/plans/a-stalled-row-says-whether-the-worker-lives.html. The row reducer in reckon/crew/recovery.py sets state = \"dispatched\" if phase == \"starting\" else \"working\" from the pointer's stored phase, which advances only when crew observe folds the stream, so a busy worker renders dispatched for hours. Derive a non-terminal run's phase from its newest stream: a run whose newest stream (stream.jsonl, resume-*.jsonl, lane-change-*.jsonl) carries at least one record of type assistant reads working. Read the streams only through the module's existing newest-stream helpers (near RUN_STREAM_GLOBS, _newest_stream_last_record_type) rather than opening stream.jsonl by name; the stored phase stays as the fallback where no stream exists. The live MCP view's phase (reckon/mcp_views.py) reads the same derivation.",
